# Paths exempt from wrapscan (gitignore-style globs, one per line).
# Keep this list SHORT and reasoned — every entry is a hole in the boundary.

# WS1 (2026-07-23 wrapscan S1 cold review; Mike's ruling: option A). The gate
# is scoped to the doctrine surface (docs/method/, docs/build/, docs/decisions/
# bodies) by EXPLICIT CI path — ci.yml never walks the dirs below at all, so
# nothing here is what keeps the gate clean. This file is the belt-and-braces
# net for any OTHER invocation (a default docs/** scan, a local run with no
# path args): it keeps the record/log/review stores' deliberate one-line-per-
# entry format from burying the doctrine-prose signal the tool actually
# targets (the un-scoped `docs/**` baseline measured ~6:1 noise to signal).

# Session logs: one dated entry per line by design (grep-ability, one-record-
# per-line diffs), not this repo's own wrapped prose.
docs/sessions/

# Review briefs/verdicts: mostly one-line-per-entry too, but genuinely mixed
# with real prose (the S1 review itself named this caveat) — ignored here
# only as the safety net above; the CI gate proper never scans this dir, so
# no real doctrine-prose signal is lost by this entry.
docs/reviews/

# The session index: hundreds of one-line-per-session entries, some
# deliberately very long (a session's whole scope on one grep-able line).
docs/SESSIONS.md

# Harvested/archived current-truth: the same one-line-per-entry record
# format, just moved out of the hot path.
docs/ROADMAP-DONE.md
*-DONE.md
*-ARCHIVE.md

# The decisions index (WS6): a one-line-per-entry record, the same class as
# SESSIONS.md — not an ADR body — even though it lives inside
# docs/decisions/, which is otherwise inside the doctrine-surface gate scope.
docs/decisions/README.md
